      "message": "Why make this a mutable field ? This sets a private member that will be accessed on another thread – namely the connectivity thread – and that thread is already started, and you don\u0027t have a thread boundary so when you access the member on the handler thread you\u0027ll expose yourself to seeing an uninitialized member. You\u0027ll crash the system with NPE in a small percentage of cases.\n\nMutable members should be strictly reserved to the cases where they contain state that actually changes throughout the lifetime of the containing class. Here this is not the case, so it\u0027s hard to use and dangerous (and case in point, this will crash). Never use non-final members for dependency injection (or generally, never when it can be avoided at all 😜), it\u0027s just too easy to get it wrong.\n\nIt seems to me much simpler to just declare a new `isChangeEnabled` method in ConnectivityService#Dependencies and override that in the test instead. It\u0027s less code, it\u0027s easier to understand, and it won\u0027t crash the system. It\u0027s also what we do for all other dependency injections in this class and other classes in our code.",
